.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

#ifdef __CYGWIN__
#include <windows.h>

int server_winpipe_accept(HANDLE pipe_handle,
                          volatile sig_atomic_t *running);
#endif
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Waits for a client to connect to a Windows Named Pipe instance, then
converts the Win32 HANDLE to a POSIX file descriptor using
\f[CR]cygwin_attach_handle_to_fd()\f[R].
.PP
Because the pipe was created without \f[CR]FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED\f[R] (to
maintain POSIX read/write compatibility), the blocking
\f[CR]ConnectNamedPipe()\f[R] call is run in a \f[B]helper thread\f[R].
The main thread polls the completion event every 500 milliseconds and
checks the \f[B]running\f[R] flag between polls.
.PP
\f[B]Shutdown sequence:\f[R]
.PP
When \f[CR]*running\f[R] becomes 0, the function cancels the blocking
\f[CR]ConnectNamedPipe()\f[R] via
\f[CR]CancelSynchronousIo(thread)\f[R], waits up to 5 seconds for the
helper thread to exit, cleans up resources, and returns \-1 with
\f[CR]errno\f[R] set to \f[CR]EINTR\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]HANDLE\-to\-fd conversion:\f[R]
.PP
On successful client connection, \f[CR]cygwin_attach_handle_to_fd()\f[R]
is called with: \- Auto\-allocated fd (\f[CR]\-1\f[R]) \- Binary mode
(\f[CR]TRUE\f[R]) \- \f[CR]GENERIC_READ | GENERIC_WRITE\f[R] access
.PP
The resulting POSIX fd is fully compatible with \f[CR]read()\f[R],
\f[CR]write()\f[R], \f[CR]close()\f[R], and
\f[CR]protocol_read_line()\f[R] / \f[CR]protocol_write_line()\f[R].
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]pipe_handle\f[R] \(em Win32 HANDLE returned by
\f[CR]server_winpipe_create()\f[R].
Must not be \f[CR]INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]running\f[R] \(em Pointer to a volatile \f[CR]sig_atomic_t\f[R]
flag.
When the pointed\-to value becomes 0, the accept is cancelled and the
function returns \-1.
May be NULL (no shutdown check; the function blocks indefinitely until a
client connects or an error occurs).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a POSIX file descriptor (non\-negative) on success.
The caller owns the fd and should \f[CR]close()\f[R] it when done (which
also releases the underlying HANDLE).
.PP
Returns \-1 on error: \- \f[CR]errno = EINTR\f[R]: Server shutdown
(running flag became 0).
\- Other errno values: System errors from \f[CR]CreateEvent\f[R],
\f[CR]CreateThread\f[R], \f[CR]WaitForSingleObject\f[R],
\f[CR]ConnectNamedPipe\f[R], or \f[CR]cygwin_attach_handle_to_fd\f[R].
.PP
On failure after \f[CR]ConnectNamedPipe\f[R] succeeds,
\f[CR]DisconnectNamedPipe()\f[R] and \f[CR]CloseHandle()\f[R] are called
to clean up.
